    deepExplanation: "Example:\n\n```ts\ntype Session = {\n  userId: string;\n  roles: string[];\n  expiresAt: number;\n};\n\nexport function canAccess(session: Session | null, requiredRole: string) {\n  return Boolean(\n    session &&\n    session.expiresAt > Date.now() &&\n    session.roles.includes(requiredRole),\n  );\n}\n```\n\nProduction pattern:\n\n```ts\n// Prefer immutable updates and keep derived values out of stored state.\nconst state = { user: { id: \"u1\", name: \"Asha\" } };\nconst next = {\n  ...state,\n  user: { ...state.user, name: \"Maya\" },\n};\n\nconsole.log(state.user.name); // Asha\nconsole.log(next.user.name);  // Maya\n```\n\nWhy it matters: Prevents duplicated or conflicting state. Makes rendering behavior predictable. Enables testable business logic and observable production behavior. Supports scaling from a single feature to large multi-team applications.",
    productionExample: "```ts\n// Prefer immutable updates and keep derived values out of stored state.\nconst state = { user: { id: \"u1\", name: \"Asha\" } };\nconst next = {\n  ...state,\n  user: { ...state.user, name: \"Maya\" },\n};\n\nconsole.log(state.user.name); // Asha\nconsole.log(next.user.name);  // Maya\n```",
    bestPractices: ["Prefer explicit, readable code."],
    tradeOffs: "Advantages: Explicit state ownership; Predictable updates; Strong debugging options; Testable architecture; Scales when boundaries are well designed. Disadvantages: Additional abstraction and learning cost; Poorly designed global state can become tightly coupled; Cache invalidation and synchronization are complex.",
    commonMistakes: ["Confusing client state with server state.","Overusing Context for high-frequency updates.","Mutating state outside the library's supported mechanisms.","Ignoring cache invalidation.","Interview trap: 'Redux is only for global state.'","Interview trap: 'Context replaces Redux in every application.'","Interview trap: 'React Query is a global state manager.'","Interview trap: 'More memoization always improves performance.'","Interview trap: 'Frontend role checks are authorization.'"],
